1. कुप् cl. 4. P. Ā. कुप्यति, ˚ते (perf. चुकोप), to be moved or excited or agitated, Suśr.; BhP.;
to swell, heave or boil with rage or emotion, be angry, be angry with (dat.; also gen., once [R. i, 49, 7] acc.; or with उपरि and gen., e.g. तस्मै or तस्य or तस्योपरि चुकोप, he was angry with him), MBh. &c.:
Caus. P. कोप॑यति, to move, shake, agitate, RV. i, 54, 4; v, 57, 3; x, 44, 8; Suśr.;
 P. Ā. कोपयति, ˚ते, to cause to swell with anger, provoke, make angry, MBh. &c.;
